assertion  XSH.iswlower.001
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswlower() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class lower as the locale definition lists it: the 26
           lowercase letters.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswlower.002
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswlower() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the uppercase letters, the digits, the punctuation, the
           white-space characters and the controls.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswlower.003
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswlower(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswlower.004
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each lowercase letter c: iswupper(towupper(c)) is non-zero,
           towlower(towupper(c)) equals c, and iswlower(c) is non-zero while
           iswupper(c) is 0.
test       t/004-lower-upper-mapping.c

assertion  XSH.iswlower.005
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswlower() is still non-zero for the 26
           lowercase letters.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
